    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored today by **Corbin Carroll** (70.90) and **Brice Turang** (65.93), both of whom benefit from optimal batting order placement. While **Corbin Carroll** faces a formidable arm in Aaron Nola, his high score is sustained by a favorable platoon split and his elite sprint speed profile, which remains our primary engine for stealing bases. **Brice Turang** earns a strong endorsement due to the leadoff spot and a 5% wind-aided boost, which maximizes his opportunity to capitalize on the basepaths despite facing a high-efficiency reliever in Clay Holmes. Meanwhile, **Mickey Moniak** (64.52) enters the fold as a high-upside play, buoyed by a significant +14% park factor that makes him a potent selection for potential power production today.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Cole Young** (41.95) and **Henry Bolte** (41.38), both of whom hit the floor threshold but ultimately fell short of the starting criteria. **Cole Young** was the closest to cracking the lineup; however, a poor matchup against the left-handed Payton Tolle\u2014coupled with his projected bottom-third order placement\u2014stifled his efficiency score compared to the aggressive deployment of **Austin Riley** (63.57). While **Austin Riley** faces the favorable matchup of Anthony Molina, his score is tempered by a minor negative adjustment for the opposing catcher\u2019s pop time. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Gabriel Moreno** and **Josh Naylor**, both of whom are currently navigating \"Lineup Pending\" status; should their actual batting orders deviate from our projections, their efficiency ratings\u2014specifically for **Gabriel Moreno**\u2014could swing significantly given his dependence on the #3 spot.",
